OL,3,GNEWSAVolunteers clear invasive plants
OL,4,Afrom woodland
OL,5,
OL,6,FVolunteers have joined forces to clear
OL,7,Finvasive plants from a woodland.
OL,9,FResidents spent two days removing
OL,10,Frhododendrons and cherry laurel from a
OL,11,Fsite in Greenham, near Newbury,
OL,12,FBerkshire, as part of a project
OL,13,Forganised by the charity Protect Earth.
OL,15,FThe plants are popular in many gardens
OL,16,Fbut known to reduce biodiversity when
OL,17,Fthey spread through woodland and block
OL,18,Flight from reaching the forest floor.
OL,20,FGreg Loxton, who lives nearby, said the
OL,21,Fsite had become overgrown and
OL,22,Fvolunteers wanted to restore it.
OL,23,APub: 23-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
